"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThis work uses the extremely common subject of traffic violations as a microscope to reveal human selfishness, responsibility, and the unfillable gap between legal justice and moral justice.  \n\nThis work consists of six short stories and shows the process of how a  is amplified into an irreversible tragedy.  \n\nIn particular, the first story, Angel's Ears, shows how a case is distorted by social prejudice.  \n\nThe self-justification of  is the psychological root of all tragedies.  \nIt's a work that acts as a warning light for all of us.  "